  "recognition_terms": {
    "_comment": "Belgian works recognition (erkenning/agréation) wording. 'class' introduces a class number in a notice; 'proof' mentions recognition without necessarily naming one. Proof terms are matched case-insensitively WITHOUT accent folding, so accented and unaccented spellings are both listed and a bare 'agree' can never match: folding 'agréé' into 'agree' would fire on English notices that merely agree to terms. Extraction patterns stay in rust/src/recognition.rs.",
